  "notes": "Seen live 2026-10-07 in a plain headed Chrome from a residential connection, nothing submitted. /removal is a start form that posts to /removal/beginremovalidv: a requester select (the subject of the request or an authorized agent), first, optional middle and last name, an email address, an authorization checkbox, an hCaptcha widget and a Send Request button. The page says the site then emails a link to the real opt-out form (valid for 24 hours), which asks for the details on the record and ends on a confirmation page and a confirmation email, with removal taking up to 3 days. That second form sits behind the email link and was not seen, so the recipe covers the start form only and a person or agent finishes the form behind the link. The old version opened a record URL and clicked buttons that this page does not have. A Playwright launched Chrome stays on a Cloudflare \"Just a moment\" page here, so a worker run may end as bot_detection. The wording the site shows after Send Request was never observed, so the outcome_when texts that prove the request went through are guesses, and the recipe stays unverified until a real submission has been seen.",
